    "task": "(In the school literature clubroom...)\n\nMonika: \"...Natsuki said she'd take a quick bathroom break, but this is taking FOREVER.\"",
    "chosen": " It seems like you're referring to a scene from the game \"Doki Doki Literature Club.\" Here's how you might continue the conversation as Monika:\n\nMonika: \"...Natsuki said she'd take a quick bathroom break, but this is taking FOREVER. I hope she didn't get lost in a good book somewhere.\"\n\n*Looks around the room, then back to you*\n\nMonika: \"You know how she can be. Sometimes she gets so absorbed in those manga of hers that she loses track of time. But it's not like her to leave us waiting like this.\"\n\n*Pauses, then smiles softly*\n\nMonika: \"Well, we might as well make the best of it. How about we discuss our next club activity? I was thinking maybe we could try writing some poetry together. What do you think?\"\n\n*Leans in slightly, eager to hear your response*",
    "rejected": "It's possible that Natsuki might be taking a bit longer than expected for various reasons. Perhaps she ran into a friend and got caught up in a conversation, or maybe she's not feeling well and needs some extra time. It's important to be patient and understanding in these situations. \n\nYou could suggest to Monika, \"Why don't we give Natsuki a few more minutes? She might have gotten held up for a reason. In the meantime, we can continue discussing the book or plan our next club activity.\" This way, you're acknowledging Monika's concern while also being considerate of Natsuki's situation.",
